/** @mainpage Qore nats Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section natsintro nats Module Introduction

    The \c nats module provides NATS messaging support for %Qore, wrapping the
    <a href="https://github.com/nats-io/nats.c">nats.c</a> client library. It supports
    core NATS publish/subscribe and request/reply messaging, JetStream persistent messaging
    with stream and consumer management, and JetStream Key-Value stores.

    To use this module, use \c "%requires nats" in your code for the binary module classes
    and \c "%requires NatsUtil" for high-level convenience classes including channel-based
    async subscriptions.

    @section natsreqs Requirements

    - <b>Qore 2.0+</b>
    - <b>nats.c library</b> (libnats)
      - Ubuntu/Debian: build from source or use a PPA
      - Fedora/RHEL: build from source
      - Alpine: build from source

    @section natsbuilding Building

    @verbatim
mkdir build
cd build
cmake ..
make
sudo make install
    @endverbatim

    To build with a specific Qore installation:
    @verbatim
cmake -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr/local ..
    @endverbatim

    @section natsarch Architecture

    The module has three layers:

    - <b>Binary module (\c nats.so)</b>: C++ QPP wrapping \c libnats for connection
      management, publish/subscribe, request/reply, JetStream, and Key-Value store.
      Provides @ref Qore::Nats::NatsConnection, @ref Qore::Nats::NatsSubscription,
      @ref Qore::Nats::JetStreamContext, and @ref Qore::Nats::NatsKeyValueStore.
    - <b>Qore module (\c NatsUtil)</b>: Pure %Qore providing high-level convenience
      classes. Provides @ref Nats::NatsClient, @ref Nats::NatsChannelSubscription,
      and @ref Nats::NatsHelper.
    - <b>Data provider modules</b>: @ref natsdp "NatsDataProvider" and
      @ref natsjetdp "NatsJetStreamDataProvider" for integration with Qore's data
      provider framework.

    @section natscorequickstart Core NATS

    @subsection natspubsub Publish / Subscribe

    The fundamental NATS messaging pattern. Publishers send messages to subjects;
    subscribers receive messages on matching subjects.

    @code{.py}
%requires NatsUtil

NatsClient client("nats://localhost:4222");

# Subscribe using channel-based async subscription
NatsChannelSubscription sub = client.channelSubscribe("events.>");

# Publish a message
client.publishString("events.log", "Hello NATS!");

# Receive the message
*hash<NatsMsgInfo> msg = sub.recv(5s);
if (msg) {
    printf("Received on %s: %s\n", msg.subject, msg.data.toString());
}

sub.close();
client.close();
    @endcode

    @subsection natsreqrep Request / Reply

    Synchronous request/reply using the @ref Nats::NatsClient::requestString()
    "NatsClient::requestString()" method.

    @code{.py}
%requires NatsUtil

NatsClient client("nats://localhost:4222");

# Set up a responder in the background
NatsChannelSubscription sub = client.channelSubscribe("service.echo");
background sub () {
    foreach hash<NatsMsgInfo> msg in (sub) {
        if (msg.reply) {
            client.publishString(msg.reply, "Echo: " + msg.data.toString());
        }
    }
}();

# Send a request and wait for the reply
string reply = client.requestString("service.echo", "Hello!", 5s);
printf("Reply: %s\n", reply);

sub.close();
client.close();
    @endcode

    @subsection natsqueuegroups Queue Groups

    Messages published to a subject are load-balanced across subscribers in the same
    queue group. Only one subscriber in the group receives each message.

    @code{.py}
NatsClient client("nats://localhost:4222");
NatsChannelSubscription sub1 = client.channelQueueSubscribe("work.tasks", "workers");
NatsChannelSubscription sub2 = client.channelQueueSubscribe("work.tasks", "workers");

# Each published message goes to exactly one worker
for (int i = 0; i < 10; ++i) {
    client.publishString("work.tasks", sprintf("task-%d", i));
}
    @endcode

    @subsection natswildcards Wildcard Subscriptions

    NATS supports two wildcards in subject subscriptions:

    - \c * matches a single token: \c "events.*" matches \c "events.log" but not
      \c "events.log.error"
    - \c > matches one or more tokens (must be last): \c "events.>" matches
      \c "events.log", \c "events.log.error", etc.

    @code{.py}
# Match any single token
NatsChannelSubscription sub1 = client.channelSubscribe("orders.*");

# Match all tokens from this point
NatsChannelSubscription sub2 = client.channelSubscribe("events.>");
    @endcode

    @subsection natscallbacksub Callback-Based Subscriptions

    For simple message processing, use callback-based subscriptions that run in a
    background thread:

    @code{.py}
%requires NatsUtil

NatsClient client("nats://localhost:4222");

# Subscribe with a callback — messages are delivered in a background thread
NatsChannelSubscription sub = client.subscribe("events.>", sub (hash<NatsMsgInfo> msg) {
    printf("Got %s: %s\n", msg.subject, msg.data.toString());
});

# Do other work while messages are processed in the background
sleep(10s);

sub.close();
client.close();
    @endcode

    @subsection natserrorhandling Error Handling

    NATS operations raise exceptions on failure. Exception codes follow the pattern
    \c NATS-<CATEGORY>-ERROR:

    |!Exception|!Description
    |\c NATS-CONNECTION-ERROR|Connection or configuration failures
    |\c NATS-PUBLISH-ERROR|Publish failures
    |\c NATS-SUBSCRIBE-ERROR|Subscription failures
    |\c NATS-REQUEST-ERROR|Request/reply failures
    |\c NATS-TIMEOUT-ERROR|Operation timeouts (request, nextMsg)
    |\c NATS-JETSTREAM-ERROR|JetStream operation failures (includes JetStream error code)
    |\c NATS-KV-ERROR|Key-Value store failures
    |\c NATS-AUTH-ERROR|Authentication failures
    |\c NATS-TLS-ERROR|TLS/SSL failures

    @code{.py}
%requires NatsUtil

try {
    NatsClient client("nats://invalid-host:4222");
} catch (hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
    if (ex.err == "NATS-CONNECTION-ERROR") {
        printf("Failed to connect: %s\n", ex.desc);
    }
}

NatsClient client("nats://localhost:4222");
try {
    # Request with a short timeout
    string reply = client.requestString("service.echo", "hello", 500ms);
} catch (hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
    if (ex.err == "NATS-TIMEOUT-ERROR") {
        printf("Request timed out: %s\n", ex.desc);
    }
}

JetStreamContext js = client.getConnection().jetStream();
try {
    # Try to get info on a non-existent stream
    js.getStreamInfo("NONEXISTENT");
} catch (hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
    if (ex.err == "NATS-JETSTREAM-ERROR") {
        printf("JetStream error: %s\n", ex.desc);
    }
}
    @endcode

    @subsection natsconnvsclient NatsConnection vs NatsClient

    The module provides two levels of API:

    - @ref Qore::Nats::NatsConnection "NatsConnection" (binary module): Low-level connection
      providing binary publish/subscribe, request/reply, and access to JetStream and KV
      contexts. Use this when you need direct control or when working with binary data.
    - @ref Nats::NatsClient "NatsClient" (NatsUtil module): High-level client wrapping
      \c NatsConnection with convenience methods for string operations, channel-based
      async subscriptions, and callback-based subscriptions. Use this for most applications.

    @code{.py}
# Low-level: binary publish + sync poll
NatsConnection conn("nats://localhost:4222");
conn.publish("events.log", binary("hello"));
NatsSubscription sub = conn.subscribe("events.>");
*hash<NatsMsgInfo> msg = sub.nextMsg(5s);
sub.unsubscribe();
conn.close();

# High-level: string publish + async channel subscription
NatsClient client("nats://localhost:4222");
client.publishString("events.log", "hello");
NatsChannelSubscription csub = client.channelSubscribe("events.>");
foreach hash<NatsMsgInfo> msg in (csub) {
    process(msg);
}
client.close();
    @endcode

    @note \c NatsClient.getConnection() returns the underlying @ref Qore::Nats::NatsConnection
    for accessing JetStream and KV store APIs.

    @section natsjetstream JetStream

    JetStream provides persistent messaging with at-least-once and exactly-once delivery
    guarantees, stream management, consumer management, and replay capabilities.

    @subsection natsjsstreams Stream Management

    Streams capture and store messages published to matching subjects.

    @code{.py}
%requires nats

NatsConnection conn("nats://localhost:4222");
JetStreamContext js = conn.jetStream();

# Create a stream
hash<NatsStreamInfo> info = js.addStream(<NatsStreamConfig>{
    "name": "ORDERS",
    "subjects": ("orders.>",),
    "retention": NATS_RETENTION_LIMITS,
    "storage": NATS_STORAGE_FILE,
    "max_msgs": 1000000,
});

# Get stream info
info = js.getStreamInfo("ORDERS");
printf("Messages: %d, Bytes: %d\n", info.messages, info.bytes);

# Purge all messages
js.purgeStream("ORDERS");

# Delete the stream
js.deleteStream("ORDERS");
    @endcode

    @subsection natsjsconsumers Consumer Management

    Consumers track message delivery state for subscribers.

    @code{.py}
hash<NatsConsumerInfo> ci = js.addConsumer("ORDERS", <NatsConsumerConfig>{
    "durable_name": "order-processor",
    "ack_policy": NATS_ACK_EXPLICIT,
    "deliver_policy": NATS_DELIVER_ALL,
});

ci = js.getConsumerInfo("ORDERS", "order-processor");
printf("Pending: %d\n", ci.num_pending);

js.deleteConsumer("ORDERS", "order-processor");
    @endcode

    @subsection natsjspubsub JetStream Publish and Subscribe

    JetStream publish returns an acknowledgment confirming the message was persisted.
    JetStream subscriptions support push and pull delivery modes with explicit
    message acknowledgment.

    @code{.py}
# Publish with acknowledgment
hash<NatsPubAck> ack = js.publish("orders.new", binary("order-123"));
printf("Published to stream %s, seq %d\n", ack.stream, ack.sequence);

# Push subscribe
NatsSubscription sub = js.subscribe("orders.>");
*hash<NatsMsgInfo> msg = sub.nextMsg(5s);
if (msg) {
    printf("Received: %s\n", msg.data.toString());
    sub.ack();
}

# Pull subscribe (durable consumer)
NatsSubscription pull_sub = js.pullSubscribe("orders.>", "order-processor");
*hash<NatsMsgInfo> pull_msg = pull_sub.nextMsg(5s);
if (pull_msg) {
    pull_sub.ack();
}
    @endcode

    @subsection natsjsacknowledgment Message Acknowledgment

    JetStream subscriptions support several acknowledgment operations:

    |!Method|!Description
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NatsSubscription::ack() "ack()"|Acknowledge successful processing
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NatsSubscription::nak() "nak()"|Negative acknowledgment (request redelivery)
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NatsSubscription::inProgress() "inProgress()"|Signal processing is ongoing (reset redelivery timer)
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NatsSubscription::term() "term()"|Terminate delivery (message will not be redelivered)

    @section natskv Key-Value Store

    JetStream provides a distributed Key-Value store built on streams.

    @code{.py}
NatsConnection conn("nats://localhost:4222");
JetStreamContext js = conn.jetStream();

# Create a KV bucket
NatsKeyValueStore kv = js.createKeyValue(<NatsKVConfig>{
    "bucket": "config",
    "history": 5,
    "ttl": 3600000,
});

# Put values
int rev1 = kv.putString("app.name", "MyApp");
int rev2 = kv.putString("app.version", "1.0");

# Get a value
*hash<NatsKVEntry> entry = kv.get("app.name");
if (entry) {
    printf("Key: %s, Value: %s, Rev: %d\n",
        entry.key, entry.value.toString(), entry.revision);
}

# Compare-and-swap update
int rev3 = kv.update("app.name", binary("NewApp"), rev1);

# List all keys
list<string> keys = kv.keys();

# Get revision history
list<hash<NatsKVEntry>> hist = kv.history("app.name");

# Soft-delete and purge
kv.delete("app.version");
kv.purge("app.version");

# Delete the bucket
js.deleteKeyValue("config");
    @endcode

    @section natstls TLS Connections

    The module supports TLS-encrypted connections using the @ref Qore::Nats::NatsTlsOptions
    "NatsTlsOptions" hashdecl.

    @code{.py}
NatsConnection conn(<NatsConnectionOptions>{
    "url": "tls://nats.example.com:4222",
    "tls": <NatsTlsOptions>{
        "ca_cert": "/path/to/ca.crt",
        "client_cert": "/path/to/client.crt",
        "client_key": "/path/to/client.key",
    },
});
    @endcode

    @section natsauth Authentication

    The module supports several authentication methods:

    @subsection natsauthtokenauth Token Authentication
    @code{.py}
NatsConnection conn(<NatsConnectionOptions>{
    "url": "nats://localhost:4222",
    "token": "secret-token",
});
    @endcode

    @subsection natsauthuserpass Username/Password Authentication
    @code{.py}
NatsConnection conn(<NatsConnectionOptions>{
    "url": "nats://localhost:4222",
    "username": "user",
    "password": "pass",
});
    @endcode

    @subsection natsauthnkey NKey Authentication
    @code{.py}
NatsConnection conn(<NatsConnectionOptions>{
    "url": "nats://localhost:4222",
    "nkey_seed": "/path/to/seed.nk",
});
    @endcode

    @subsection natsauthcreds Credentials File Authentication
    @code{.py}
NatsConnection conn(<NatsConnectionOptions>{
    "url": "nats://localhost:4222",
    "credentials": "/path/to/creds.creds",
});
    @endcode

    @section natsdp NatsDataProvider Module

    The \c NatsDataProvider module integrates core NATS messaging into Qore's data provider
    framework. Use \c "%requires NatsDataProvider" to load the module.

    @subsection natsdp_hierarchy Provider Hierarchy

    @verbatim
<root>
  +-- publish          (NatsPublishDataProvider -- DPAT_API)
  +-- request          (NatsRequestDataProvider -- DPAT_API)
  +-- subscribe        (NatsSubscribeEventDataProvider -- DPAT_EVENT)
  +-- queue-subscribe  (NatsQueueSubscribeEventDataProvider -- DPAT_EVENT)
    @endverbatim

    @subsection natsdp_connections Connection Schemes

    |!Scheme|!Transport|!Example URL
    |\c nats://|Plaintext NATS|\c nats://localhost:4222
    |\c tls://|TLS-encrypted NATS|\c tls://nats.example.com:4222

    @subsection natsdp_cli Command Line Usage

    @verbatim
# Publish a message
qdp 'nats{url=nats://localhost:4222}/publish' dor subject=events.log,data=hello

# Send a request
qdp 'nats{url=nats://localhost:4222}/request' dor subject=service.echo,data=hello
    @endverbatim

    @section natsjetdp NatsJetStreamDataProvider Module

    The \c NatsJetStreamDataProvider module integrates NATS JetStream into Qore's data
    provider framework. Use \c "%requires NatsJetStreamDataProvider" to load the module.

    @subsection natsjetdp_hierarchy Provider Hierarchy

    @verbatim
<root>
  +-- streams
  |   +-- create     (NatsJSStreamCreateDataProvider -- DPAT_API)
  |   +-- delete     (NatsJSStreamDeleteDataProvider -- DPAT_API)
  |   +-- info       (NatsJSStreamInfoDataProvider -- DPAT_API)
  |   +-- purge      (NatsJSStreamPurgeDataProvider -- DPAT_API)
  +-- consumers
  |   +-- create     (NatsJSConsumerCreateDataProvider -- DPAT_API)
  |   +-- delete     (NatsJSConsumerDeleteDataProvider -- DPAT_API)
  |   +-- info       (NatsJSConsumerInfoDataProvider -- DPAT_API)
  +-- publish        (NatsJSPublishDataProvider -- DPAT_API)
  +-- subscribe      (NatsJSSubscribeEventDataProvider -- DPAT_EVENT)
  +-- pull-subscribe (NatsJSPullSubscribeEventDataProvider -- DPAT_EVENT)
  +-- kv
      +-- put        (NatsJSKVPutDataProvider -- DPAT_API)
      +-- get        (NatsJSKVGetDataProvider -- DPAT_API)
      +-- delete     (NatsJSKVDeleteDataProvider -- DPAT_API)
      +-- keys       (NatsJSKVKeysDataProvider -- DPAT_API)
      +-- history    (NatsJSKVHistoryDataProvider -- DPAT_API)
    @endverbatim

    @subsection natsjetdp_cli Command Line Usage

    @verbatim
# Create a stream
qdp 'natsjetstream{url=nats://localhost:4222}/streams/create' dor name=ORDERS,subjects=orders.>

# Publish to JetStream
qdp 'natsjetstream{url=nats://localhost:4222}/publish' dor subject=orders.new,data=order-123

# Put a KV value
qdp 'natsjetstream{url=nats://localhost:4222}/kv/put' dor bucket=config,key=app.name,value=MyApp

# Get a KV value
qdp 'natsjetstream{url=nats://localhost:4222}/kv/get' dor bucket=config,key=app.name
    @endverbatim

    @section natshashdecls Hashdecl Reference

    The following hashdecls are defined in the \c Qore::Nats namespace:

    |!Hashdecl|!Description
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NatsConnectionOptions "NatsConnectionOptions"|Connection options
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NatsTlsOptions "NatsTlsOptions"|TLS configuration options
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NatsMsgInfo "NatsMsgInfo"|Received message information
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NatsStreamConfig "NatsStreamConfig"|JetStream stream configuration
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NatsStreamInfo "NatsStreamInfo"|JetStream stream information
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NatsConsumerConfig "NatsConsumerConfig"|JetStream consumer configuration
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NatsConsumerInfo "NatsConsumerInfo"|JetStream consumer information
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NatsPubAck "NatsPubAck"|JetStream publish acknowledgment
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NatsKVConfig "NatsKVConfig"|Key-Value bucket configuration
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NatsKVEntry "NatsKVEntry"|Key-Value entry

    @section natsconstants Constants

    @subsection natsretentionpolicies Retention Policies

    |!Constant|!Value|!Description
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NATS_RETENTION_LIMITS|0|Retain based on limits (max messages, bytes, age)
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NATS_RETENTION_INTEREST|1|Retain until acknowledged by all consumers
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NATS_RETENTION_WORKQUEUE|2|Retain until acknowledged (work queue)

    @subsection natsstoragetypes Storage Types

    |!Constant|!Value|!Description
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NATS_STORAGE_FILE|0|File-based storage
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NATS_STORAGE_MEMORY|1|Memory-based storage

    @subsection natsdiscardpolicies Discard Policies

    |!Constant|!Value|!Description
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NATS_DISCARD_OLD|0|Discard old messages when full
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NATS_DISCARD_NEW|1|Reject new messages when full

    @subsection natsackpolicies Ack Policies

    |!Constant|!Value|!Description
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NATS_ACK_NONE|0|No acknowledgment required
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NATS_ACK_ALL|1|All messages must be acknowledged
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NATS_ACK_EXPLICIT|2|Each message acknowledged individually

    @subsection natsdeliverpolicies Deliver Policies

    |!Constant|!Value|!Description
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NATS_DELIVER_ALL|0|Deliver all available messages
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NATS_DELIVER_LAST|1|Start with the last message
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NATS_DELIVER_NEW|2|Deliver only new messages
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NATS_DELIVER_BY_START_SEQUENCE|3|Start from a specific sequence
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NATS_DELIVER_BY_START_TIME|4|Start from a specific time
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NATS_DELIVER_LAST_PER_SUBJECT|5|Last message per subject

    @subsection natsreplaypolicies Replay Policies

    |!Constant|!Value|!Description
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NATS_REPLAY_INSTANT|0|Replay as fast as possible
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NATS_REPLAY_ORIGINAL|1|Replay at original delivery rate

    @subsection natskvoperations Key-Value Operations

    |!Constant|!Value|!Description
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NATS_KV_OP_PUT|1|Put or update operation
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NATS_KV_OP_DELETE|2|Delete operation
    |@ref Qore::Nats::NATS_KV_OP_PURGE|3|Purge operation

    @section natsrelnotes Release Notes

    @subsection nats_v1_0 nats Module Version 1.0

    <b>Dependencies</b>: \c libnats (nats.c client library)

    <b>Features</b>:
    - initial release
    - @ref Qore::Nats::NatsConnection "NatsConnection": connect to NATS servers with
      URL or options hash; supports token, username/password, NKey, and credentials
      file authentication; supports TLS
    - @ref Qore::Nats::NatsSubscription "NatsSubscription": subscribe to subjects with
      wildcard support (\c * and \c >); queue group subscriptions for load balancing;
      auto-unsubscribe and drain support
    - @ref Qore::Nats::JetStreamContext "JetStreamContext": stream and consumer CRUD;
      JetStream publish with acknowledgment; push and pull subscriptions
    - @ref Qore::Nats::NatsKeyValueStore "NatsKeyValueStore": put, get, create, update
      (CAS), delete, purge, keys, and history operations
    - hashdecls for all configuration and result types
    - constants for JetStream retention, storage, discard, ack, deliver, and replay policies
    - @ref Nats::NatsClient "NatsClient": high-level client with string publish/request,
      channel-based async subscriptions, and callback-based subscriptions
    - @ref Nats::NatsChannelSubscription "NatsChannelSubscription": channel-based async
      subscription with iterator support, timeout receive, and \c channel_select()
      multiplexing
    - @ref Nats::NatsHelper "NatsHelper": subject validation and URL parsing utilities
    - \c NatsDataProvider module: data provider API for core NATS publish, request,
      subscribe, and queue-subscribe; connection schemes \c nats:// and \c tls://;
      action catalog registration
    - \c NatsJetStreamDataProvider module: data provider API for JetStream streams,
      consumers, publish, push/pull subscribe, and Key-Value store operations;
      action catalog registration

